(Regression test for bug #68: the headline repro. The *expression* form of
 a format hole - `"{element 2 of nested}"` - threw away the runtime tag the
 element load had just put in r11 and rendered the payload as an integer,
 so a nested-list element printed a LIVE HEAP ADDRESS that changed between
 runs. The very same read printed as a statement was correct, which is what
 proves the tag was there and simply not consulted.

 Acceptance: the hole and the statement agree, on the same element, in the
 same run - and the answer is the rendering, not an address.)

a list called nested is [1, [2, 3], "four"].

Print "{element 2 of nested}".
Print element 2 of nested.

Print "{element 3 of nested}".
Print element 3 of nested.
